This is a simple Python implementation of the Genetic Algorithm demonstration at www.ai-junkie.com
The original code was in C++. I felt the need of coding the thing myself, and decided to do it in Python.

The problem we solve is:
    "For any given 'target' number, find an expression invlolving any legal combination of 
    addition(+), subtraction(-), multiplication(*) and division(/) on digits that represents the 
    given target number.

    e.g., for the target 15, "9 + 3 * 2" is a solution."

    **Important: In Fup's code, the evaluation of the expressions generated was simple, left to right
    evaluation. I have used normal arithmetic precedence based evaluation(see `expr.py')

===============================================================================
strategy/ -- GA-evolved long-only trading entry signals
===============================================================================

A second, unrelated use of the same genetic-algorithm idea: instead of
evolving a bit-string that decodes to an arithmetic expression, it evolves a
real-valued genome that decodes to a long-only entry rule (an AND of
indicator conditions) plus a risk model (ATR stop, R-multiple target, max
holding period). Fitness is "Edge": a Wilson-confidence-adjusted expectancy
in R-multiples, computed from realized trades in an actual bar-by-bar
backtest -- not a curve fit to a single number.

Quickstart (synthetic data, no external dependencies beyond pandas/numpy):

    python3 -m venv .venv && ./.venv/bin/pip install -r requirements.txt
    ./.venv/bin/python -m strategy.run_discovery --source synthetic

This runs the GA per synthetic symbol, evolves entry rules on the first 70%
of the data, re-tests each surviving rule on the held-out last 30%
(walk-forward validation -- the only real defense against reporting a
curve-fit rule as having edge), and writes every discovered rule plus its
in-sample and out-of-sample stats to output/strategies/latest.json.
Rules that keep a positive edge out-of-sample are flagged
"validated_out_of_sample": true; most won't be, and that's expected --
finding a real, robust long-only edge is supposed to be hard.

Real data (once Supabase is connected in this workspace):

    export SUPABASE_URL="https://<project>.supabase.co"
    export SUPABASE_KEY="<key>"
    ./.venv/bin/python -m strategy.run_discovery --source supabase \
        --table ohlcv_daily --symbols BTCUSD,ETHUSD

See strategy/data.py for the expected table shape (symbol, timestamp, open,
high, low, close, volume -- remap column names via --symbol-col/--timestamp-col
or a col_map if the real schema differs).

Module layout:
    strategy/indicators.py     SMA/EMA/RSI/MACD/Bollinger/ADX/Stochastic/ATR
    strategy/genome.py         real-coded chromosome <-> entry-rule decoding
    strategy/backtest.py       long-only trade simulator (next-bar-open fills)
    strategy/fitness.py        Edge = Wilson-lower-bound-adjusted expectancy
    strategy/ga_engine.py      the GA loop itself (selection/crossover/mutation)
    strategy/interpretation.py plain-English rationale per archetype combo
    strategy/slicer.py         chronological train/test split
    strategy/data.py           Supabase / CSV / synthetic-demo data loading
    strategy/export.py         JSON schema matching the planned Supabase table
    strategy/run_discovery.py  CLI that ties it all together

